Development Authority for an RCC drain and road at Sector Kappa-2**, valued at Rs 38.23 crore. The filing states the award still depends on a Letter of Acceptance and an executed agreement _(~49.0% of mcap)_.","**OM Infra** - joint venture MCC-Om secures a **Rs 32.18 crore work order from the Vidarbha Irrigation Development Corporation** for a lift irrigation scheme feeding the Ghodazari tank under the Gosikhurd project, to run 12 months _(~4.2% of mcap)_.","**GPT Infraprojects** - wholly-owned Alcon Builders and Engineers is **declared lowest bidder in a Rs 21.21 crore Western Railway order** to design, supply and commission electronic interlocking at Viramgam in the Ahmedabad division _(~1.4% of mcap)_.","**Popular Foundations** - receives a **Rs 18.15 crore order excluding GST from Rajalakshmi Institute of Technology** to build the superstructure of a G+7 block at Kuthambakkam, Chennai, within 380 days _(~31.7% of mcap)_.","**Yaan Enterprises** - receives a **purchase order worth about Rs 15.86 crore for yellow maize from the State Agri Horticultural Development Co-operative Society, Thiruvananthapuram**, with Rs 3 crore taken as advance and supply due in two months _(~39.1% of mcap)_.","**RailTel Corporation of India** - wins a **Rs 14.09 crore work order including tax from Uttar Pradesh University of Medical Sciences** for a five-year, outcome-linked hospital information management system on a pay-per-use basis, running to September 2031.","**Cranex** - receives **two orders aggregating Rs 7.18 crore**: a Rs 1.33 crore Letter of Award from BHEL Chanju for 100-tonne double-girder cranes for the 3x16 MW Chanju Stage III hydro project, and a Rs 5.84 crore order from DEE VEE Projects for six materials-handling systems _(~12.1% of mcap)_.","**Annu Projects** - receives a **Rs 5.04 crore Letter of Acceptance from East Central Railway's Samastipur division** for laying optical fibre and quad cable and providing alternate communication across the SPJ section, over 12 months _(~1.5% of mcap)_.","**Prostarm Info Systems** - receives a **Rs 3.67 crore purchase order from Rayzon Energy** to supply and install 2,400 kVA and 500 kVA uninterruptible power systems with batteries and panels, for delivery in five to six weeks.","**Skytech Infinite Platform** - receives **purchase orders totalling Rs 3.15 crore excluding tax to design, supply and commission PLC automation panels for three Karnataka rural water-supply villages**; the customer is withheld for confidentiality _(~12.1% of mcap)_.","**Cosmic CRF** - subsidiary N.S. Engineering Projects **bags purchase orders of Rs 2.50 crore including GST from a Kolkata infrastructure and steel customer** for 150 tonnes each of fabricated MS beams and hollow square bar, to ship within two weeks.","**Chiraharit** - receives a **Rs 77.18 lakh purchase order from Larsen & Toubro** for pipes and fittings for a solar module cleaning system, to be supplied in Bihar.","**Iware Supplychain Services** - signs a **12-month service agreement with Emami Agrotech for warehousing, handling and end-to-end transportation from its Kandla plant into Punjab**; no contract value is given because the rates are per tonne and volumes depend on the client's dispatch plans.","**Admach Systems** - **completes a Rs 10.62 crore nuclear fuel flow control systems project for the Nuclear Fuel Complex, Hyderabad**, three weeks inside its 15 October deadline; the order itself was placed in December 2025 _(~3.6% of mcap)_."],"fund_raises_fresh_equity":["**Qualitek Labs** - board approves a **preferential issue of 3,86,000 equity shares and 5,20,000 convertible warrants at Rs 518.55, Rs 20.02 crore and Rs 26.96 crore respectively, Rs 46.98 crore together (our arithmetic)**, with **Ashish Kacholia** taking 1,73,200 shares among 26 allottees; subject to an EGM on 16 October.","**Manba Finance** - board approves a **preferential issue of up to Rs 99.99 crore** - Rs 67.50 crore of equity at Rs 135 to non-promoters and Rs 32.50 crore of warrants to the promoter group - to fund its lending book, subject to members' approval and an increase in authorised capital to Rs 65 crore.","**Rama Steel Tubes** - board approves **Rs 140 crore of preferential equity at Rs 5 a share plus a Rs 166.40 crore share swap** to pay for 21.62% of Automech Group Holding, and Rs 40 crore of promoter warrants, all subject to an extraordinary general meeting _(~19.5% of mcap)_."],"equity_allotments":["**Fredun Pharmaceuticals** - allots **3,61,599 equity shares on conversion of 1,20,533 warrants** held by Alchemy Capital Management and nine others, the entitlement having tripled after a 1:2 bonus issue; a past conversion, not new money.","**PC Jeweller** - allots **74,07,500 equity shares to promoter and managing director Balram Garg on conversion of warrants**, against the balance Rs 10.00 crore at Rs 13.50 a warrant, lifting promoter holding from 38.76% to 38.80%; 4,82,14,722 warrants remain unconverted."],"m_and_a":["**Fredun Pharmaceuticals** - acquires a **26% stake in Goodman Vetcare, a Mumbai pet pharmacy chain the release values at Rs 300 crore**, whose revenue it puts at Rs 23.6 crore in FY26 against Rs 14.1 crore in FY24. The consideration paid is not disclosed.","**Maithan Alloys** - buys **3,30,000 shares, or 0.05%, of One 97 Communications (Paytm) on the exchange for Rs 60.19 crore**, disclosed on crossing the Regulation 30 threshold and described as an investment with no intent to acquire control.","**Maithan Alloys** - separately buys **11,730 shares, or 0.01%, of ESDS Software Solution for Rs 1.90 crore** on the same day, again as a treasury investment rather than a controlling stake.","**Jammu & Kashmir Bank** - signs an **escrow agreement with MetLife International Holdings and three Barclays entities to complete the sale of its 0.5% stake in PNB MetLife India Insurance at Rs 117.20 a share, Rs 120.10 crore**, under a share purchase agreement dated 17 July."],"capex_core":["**Borosil Renewables** - board approves a **revised cost of up to Rs 1,100 crore, from Rs 950 crore, for two 300 TPD furnaces at Bharuch** and moves commissioning to end-March 2027 from December 2026, citing Middle East supply-chain disruption and a widened scope; capacity goes from 1,000 to 1,600 TPD _(~16.6% of mcap)_.","**Borosil Scientific** - approves a **Rs 60 crore second manufacturing facility at Bharuch**, lifting glassware capacity from about 15 lakh units a year to about 108 lakh, with commercial production expected by March 2027 _(~5.7% of mcap)_.","**Borosil** - **hands its own planned Rs 42 crore Bharuch glassware plant to Borosil Scientific**, which will now build and fund it; Borosil's requirement continues to be met through the existing manufacturing arrangement between the two.","**Solex Energy** - tells its AGM it will **invest about Rs 4,000 crore between FY27 and FY30 to add 2.2 GW of solar cell capacity by FY28, 5.2 GW by early FY29 and a first 5 GWh of battery assembly by FY29**, on FY26 revenue of Rs 1,621 crore and order visibility above Rs 3,400 crore.","**TruAlt Bioenergy** - board approves **further equity investments of Rs 21.42 crore in Leafiniti Bioenergy and Rs 8.27 crore in TruAlt Sumi Gas**, both existing subsidiaries, and appoints Dr Sarvamangala R Patil an additional independent director."],"credit_rating_changes":["**Aadhar Housing Finance** - **ICRA upgrades it to AA+ and revises the outlook to Stable from Positive** across Rs 2,231.63 crore of debentures, Rs 1,350 crore of bank facilities and Rs 60 crore of subordinated debt, and withdraws the rating on Rs 504.40 crore of debentures that have been redeemed.","**Shanti Inorganics** - **CRISIL upgrades it to BBB/Stable from BBB-/Stable and to A3+ from A3** on Rs 66.05 crore of bank facilities, citing 21% compound revenue growth over five years and a capacity rise to 1,15,000 tonnes a year from 36,800.","**Solar Industries India** - **CRISIL places its AA+ ratings on Rating Watch with Developing Implications** across Rs 1,479.50 crore of bank facilities and Rs 35 crore of debentures, after the company's 14 September announcement of a proposed acquisition of South Africa's Omnia Holdings at an enterprise value the agency puts at about Rs 12,951 crore.","**Seamec** - **CRISIL removes its A+ and A1 ratings from Rating Watch with Developing Implications and reaffirms them**, across Rs 863 crore of bank facilities."],"business_updates":["**Results season** — 23 companies filed results / earnings-call material today (press releases, recordings, transcripts, presentations) — tracked in the Results tab, not itemised here.","**Cupid** - tells its AGM that **FY26 total income rose 93% to Rs 391 crore and profit after tax 165% to Rs 108 crore**, and guides to Rs 725-750 crore of revenue and Rs 210-225 crore of profit in FY27, with its 170,000 sq ft Palava plant due to commission next quarter.","**Indian Emulsifiers** - signs a **non-binding memorandum of understanding with Spice Lounge Food Works for exclusive Indian offtake of its new food-grade emulsifier line**, indicatively 200 tonnes a month on a take-or-pay basis for five years. Pricing and volumes are not settled and the company says no revenue accrues until a definitive agreement is signed."]},"theme_titles":{"order_wins":"Order wins (notable vs mcap)","fund_raises_fresh_equity":"Fund raises (fresh equity)","equity_allotments":"Equity allotments (new)","m_and_a":"M&A / restructuring","capex_core":"Capex (core / topline)","credit_rating_changes":"Credit-rating changes","business_updates":"Business updates"},"theme_rows":{"order_wins":[{"label":"SUGSLLOYD","ticker":"SUGSLLOYD","company":"Sugs Lloyd Ltd","isin":"INE0XX801016","pdf_link":"https://www.bseindia.com/xml-data/corpfiling/AttachLive/f83bd000-7ac5-44f1-ab12-e95f857df91e.pdf","mcap":631.4},{"label":"RITES","ticker":"RITES","company":"RITES Limited","isin":"INE320J01015","pdf_link":"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/corporate/RITES_22092026141041_IntimationSigned22092026